+// The price log (TSC_TS_SHARE_PRICE): what sharing costs, written by each checker thread once it has checked its
+// files, and replayed by scripts/share-price.mjs. It lives in this module because that is what it prices, and
+// because a module of its own would move the functions the committed profile describes, which a build then
+// cannot match.
+//
+// TSC_TS_SHARE_PRICE=<prefix> makes each checker append a record to arrays in memory: for each result it computed,
+// took or could have taken, for each translation, for each type-operator evaluation and for the interval it checked
+// in. The arrays are written to `<prefix>-c<index>-<n>.log` once the thread has checked its files, where `n` counts
+// the logs that thread wrote, so a checker whose thread was replaced by another leaves both logs. Nothing is written
+// on the hot path, and nothing at all is when the variable is unset: `priceEnabled` is then false and every caller
+// returns at its first branch.
+//
+// Times are `performance.now()` of this build, which every thread of the native runtime shares (it counts from the
+// executable's load). Each log also writes the epoch that clock stood for, `Date.now() - performance.now()` at the
+// start of the thread, so a reader can place the log on the wall clock; the runtime has no `performance.timeOrigin`.
+//
+// The log is numeric: a record is a slice of a flat array, and the few strings it needs (file names, why a result was
+// not posted) are interned in a table that is written before the records.
